  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If, in the expression \\(x^2-3,\\) \\(x\\) increases or decreases by a positive amount \\(a,\\) the expression changes by an amount:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\pm2ax+a^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2ax\\pm a^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\pm a^2-3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\((x+a)^2-3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\((x-a)^2-3\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1958-p23.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For an increase, \\[ \\begin{aligned} &(x+a)^2-3-(x^2-3)\\\\ &\\qquad=2ax+a^2. \\end{aligned} \\] For a decrease, \\[ \\begin{aligned} &(x-a)^2-3-(x^2-3)\\\\ &\\qquad=-2ax+a^2. \\end{aligned} \\] Together these changes are \\(\\pm2ax+a^2.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Compute \\(f(x+a)-f(x)\\) and \\(f(x-a)-f(x)\\) for \\(f(x)=x^2-3\\)",
        "The constant term cancels in both differences"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
